1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:07,650
[When Banai was younger,]

3
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:12,670
[she heard countless stories
told by the elder]

4
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:16,670
[of myths about the tribe.]

5
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:19,880
[So when Banai grew up,]

6
00:00:20,010 --> 00:00:24,460
[she invited the elder]

7
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:32,910
[to retell those stories
to the children of the tribe.]

8
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:37,000
[However, the aged elder]

9
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:43,910
[had forgotten the stories
he once told before.]

10
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:48,610
[The night the elder passed away,]

11
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:53,890
[the family revealed to Banai]

12
00:00:54,030 --> 00:00:59,300
[that the fairy tales the elder told her]

13
00:00:59,390 --> 00:01:05,680
[were made up to coax the children.]

14
00:01:05,770 --> 00:01:09,470
[That was because in the real world,]

15
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:14,840
[there was neither Kakarayan nor Kawas.]

16
00:01:14,970 --> 00:01:21,480
[There were only myths
and legends in this world.]

17
00:01:21,570 --> 00:01:23,110
[There was no god.]

18
00:01:44,670 --> 00:01:47,880
[As long as she has this ring,]

19
00:01:48,009 --> 00:01:52,500
[you won't forget
the promise you made to her.]

20
00:01:52,590 --> 00:01:54,920
[You'll always be by her side.]

21
00:01:55,009 --> 00:01:59,850
[You'll be constantly thinking of her
and protecting her.]

22
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:01,560
[And you'll be deeply in love with her.]

23
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:05,960
'Orad.

24
00:02:06,050 --> 00:02:08,650
Whether you like it or not,

25
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:12,250
everything you believe in and love

26
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:16,300
is all a lie!

27
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:20,990
[Episode 13, Living Each Day
That Could Be the Last]

28
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:06,930
You are

29
00:05:08,030 --> 00:05:09,220
Kakarayan?

30
00:05:15,110 --> 00:05:16,080
What's wrong?

31
00:05:17,490 --> 00:05:19,690
Why are you looking at me like that?

32
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:22,550
Why do you ask when you already know?

33
00:05:23,430 --> 00:05:25,720
You know very well what I've been through.

34
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:30,560
What I believe, what I have,

35
00:05:31,570 --> 00:05:33,420
and even my existence

36
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:38,120
are all just part of your lies.

37
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:41,250
They're the lies you used

38
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:43,180
to deceive yourself and avoid everything.

39
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:50,930
Is this the answer you're giving yourself

40
00:05:51,850 --> 00:05:53,610
after everything you've been through?

41
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:55,240
What else then?

42
00:05:55,330 --> 00:05:57,350
What do you want me to do?

43
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:59,590
I already saw it
in the Reflection of Time.

44
00:05:59,730 --> 00:06:01,530
When a lie is found out

45
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:03,380
and no one is willing
to believe it anymore,

46
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:05,800
how do you expect it to continue to exist?

47
00:06:08,830 --> 00:06:10,370
You're right.

48
00:06:11,390 --> 00:06:13,320
When a lie is found out

49
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:16,230
and no one is willing
to believe it anymore,

50
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,870
it will cease to exist.

51
00:06:21,110 --> 00:06:22,520
But have you thought

52
00:06:23,490 --> 00:06:26,350
about Hsieh Tien-ti, the woman you love?

53
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:30,970
Even when everyone around her told her

54
00:06:31,050 --> 00:06:33,170
that you were a lie that didn't exist,

55
00:06:34,090 --> 00:06:36,200
she still believed in you.

56
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:37,870
Didn't she?

57
00:06:39,810 --> 00:06:41,390
[Like right now.]

58
00:06:43,330 --> 00:06:44,960
[When you're holding my hand,]

59
00:06:45,570 --> 00:06:49,970
[your hands feel warm.]

60
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:53,670
I can feel your warmth.

61
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:55,870
There's no way...

62
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:58,020
There's no way you're fake.

63
00:07:00,050 --> 00:07:03,300
How can you be a lie?

64
00:07:03,390 --> 00:07:05,720
[You chose
what you thought was the truth.]

65
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:07,700
What about Hsieh Tien-ti then?

66
00:07:09,290 --> 00:07:11,970
Have you ever thought about

67
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:15,050
what your existence meant to her?

68
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:16,500
I...

69
00:07:16,590 --> 00:07:17,910
There's no need to answer me just yet.

70
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:22,310
Let's see what her decision is first.

71
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,640
Then you can tell me

72
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:26,760
what your answer is.

73
00:07:32,830 --> 00:07:33,880
This is

74
00:07:35,159 --> 00:07:36,390
the Reflection of Time.

75
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:38,370
[That's right.]

76
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:41,060
[What you're seeing now]

77
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:42,550
[is the Reflection of Time]

78
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,880
[of what's about to happen.]

79
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:56,810
Kakarayan.

80
00:07:58,390 --> 00:08:00,630
Your lie is gone.

81
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:02,260
Show yourself now.

82
00:08:03,890 --> 00:08:05,340
Come back now.

83
00:08:06,090 --> 00:08:07,850
Come back!

84
00:08:08,690 --> 00:08:10,270
Kakarayan!

85
00:08:12,820 --> 00:08:14,890
I...

86
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:16,690
I can weave another dream

87
00:08:16,780 --> 00:08:18,190
that will make you happy.

88
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:19,470
I won't let humans

89
00:08:19,550 --> 00:08:21,530
destroy our dream again.

90
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,770
Kakarayan.

91
00:08:23,870 --> 00:08:26,730
Come back to me, Kakarayan.

92
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:30,770
I promise I won't let you down again.

93
00:08:30,910 --> 00:08:35,750
Kakarayan!

94
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:41,200
Kakarayan!

95
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:39,630
[How many times have I told you?]

96
00:09:40,470 --> 00:09:42,090
[Watch where you're going.]

97
00:09:42,890 --> 00:09:44,290
You bumbling fool.

98
00:10:16,410 --> 00:10:17,650
[When I'm done]

99
00:10:19,190 --> 00:10:21,830
[saying what I'm about to say to you,]

100
00:10:24,510 --> 00:10:26,450
[you're going to delete this video.]

101
00:10:28,820 --> 00:10:30,670
[And all of this]

102
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:33,530
[will disappear from your memory]

103
00:10:34,150 --> 00:10:36,390
[along with it.]

104
00:10:38,330 --> 00:10:40,040
You'll forget

105
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:43,560
that 'Orad said he was a lie.

106
00:10:47,210 --> 00:10:48,840
You won't believe

107
00:10:48,930 --> 00:10:51,130
the fact that he disappeared.

108
00:10:52,930 --> 00:10:55,530
[Everything about him leaving]

109
00:10:56,670 --> 00:10:58,700
[and how all the Reflections of Time
you saw]

110
00:10:58,780 --> 00:11:00,320
[were nightmares,]

111
00:11:01,730 --> 00:11:03,540
[none of it is true.]

112
00:11:11,850 --> 00:11:14,620
So no matter what happens in the future,

113
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:17,350
make sure you remember.

114
00:11:19,330 --> 00:11:21,710
You have to believe.

115
00:11:23,860 --> 00:11:25,140
You have to believe

116
00:11:25,230 --> 00:11:27,030
that he has always been by your side.

117
00:11:31,390 --> 00:11:32,930
Even if no one believes it

118
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:35,830
and no one can see him,

119
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:37,810
don't be scared.

120
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:41,290
Because you know

121
00:11:42,870 --> 00:11:45,110
he never left.

122
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:51,230
Just like before,

123
00:11:52,550 --> 00:11:54,620
he is by your side

124
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:58,230
and he will always protect you.

125
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:45,000
What's wrong?

126
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:55,120
Nothing.

127
00:12:56,740 --> 00:13:00,310
I just had a nightmare.

128
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:04,050
What nightmare?

129
00:13:06,780 --> 00:13:07,880
I forgot.

130
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:09,680
It's like...

131
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:14,300
I think you went missing.

132
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:16,810
I went missing?

133
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:20,550
I'm here. I'm not missing.

134
00:13:22,570 --> 00:13:23,500
It's okay.

135
00:13:41,710 --> 00:13:42,900
['Orad.]

136
00:13:46,020 --> 00:13:48,400
Everything is as you said.

137
00:13:48,490 --> 00:13:52,450
[Street cleaning truck]

138
00:13:53,190 --> 00:13:57,590
It hasn't rained in months.

139
00:14:01,730 --> 00:14:02,960
We've run out of water.

140
00:14:03,050 --> 00:14:05,210
Can't you make an exception?

141
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:07,490
One bout of rain is good enough.

142
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:10,000
Okay.

143
00:14:10,530 --> 00:14:11,720
I know what you want to say.

144
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:12,950
You're going to say

145
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:14,890
you're just Kakarayan's messenger.

146
00:14:14,970 --> 00:14:16,160
If Kakarayan hadn't shown you

147
00:14:16,290 --> 00:14:18,580
this Reflection of Time...

148
00:14:19,990 --> 00:14:21,620
Why are you mad?

149
00:14:23,330 --> 00:14:25,710
I'm just asking.

150
00:14:26,370 --> 00:14:27,380
How about this?

151
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:31,430
Why don't you just give a little drizzle?

152
00:14:32,130 --> 00:14:34,290
Kakarayan wouldn't be so stingy.

153
00:14:34,770 --> 00:14:35,080
Right?

154
00:14:35,210 --> 00:14:36,360
[The command center announced today]

155
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:39,480
[that there are 57 more White Algae
Disorder cases in the country.]

156
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:40,620
[Serious side effects
from the algae vaccine trial]

157
00:14:39,570 --> 00:14:40,490
[Up until now,]

158
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:43,570
[the number of cases
has officially reached 5,000.]

159
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:45,820
[On the other hand,
the White Algae Disorder...]

160
00:14:48,370 --> 00:14:50,520
Stop watching it.

161
00:14:50,660 --> 00:14:51,840
Didn't you tell me

162
00:14:51,930 --> 00:14:54,620
not to worry
about the White Algae Disorder?

163
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:57,520
And now, you're here
watching the news alone.

164
00:14:57,610 --> 00:14:59,020
Let's eat.

165
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:04,300
Let me tell you something crazy.

166
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:08,390
Aren't you always with me these days?

167
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:11,200
I got used to

168
00:15:11,290 --> 00:15:13,930
talking to you about every little thing.

169
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:15,300
I forgot

170
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:17,850
that people around me can't see you.

171
00:15:19,390 --> 00:15:21,280
Do you know what Ms. Chang-fen

172
00:15:21,410 --> 00:15:23,220
told me in her office

173
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:24,450
this afternoon?

174
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:25,590
What?

175
00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:27,880
She said she saw me

176
00:15:27,970 --> 00:15:31,090
talking to myself many times.

177
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:36,770
She asked if I was stressed out from work.

178
00:15:36,850 --> 00:15:40,110
I'm not kidding. She looked up
all sorts of information online

179
00:15:40,200 --> 00:15:42,310
and told me

180
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:47,060
about the dissociative disorder
or something.

181
00:15:47,150 --> 00:15:49,350
She said I totally had the symptoms.

182
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:50,580
That's enough.

183
00:15:50,670 --> 00:15:51,420
You know...

184
00:15:51,550 --> 00:15:51,950
Stop talking.

185
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,130
When I heard it,

186
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:56,260
I couldn't believe it.

187
00:15:57,580 --> 00:16:00,440
So I thought of a way.

188
00:16:00,530 --> 00:16:02,290
When I feel like talking to you
from now on,

189
00:16:02,370 --> 00:16:04,270
I'll do this first.

190
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:05,630
This way,

191
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:07,920
as long as I have my phone,

192
00:16:08,010 --> 00:16:09,460
I won't have to think so much

193
00:16:09,550 --> 00:16:10,510
-when I'm talking to you.
-That's enough.

194
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:11,480
Otherwise, the person next to me

195
00:16:11,570 --> 00:16:13,950
might really think I'm crazy.

196
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,810
'Orad, look here.

197
00:16:24,370 --> 00:16:26,130
That was lame.

198
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:27,760
You wasted the film.

199
00:16:27,850 --> 00:16:30,090
It's not funny. I want a proper photo.

200
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:32,420
Go over there.

201
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:35,590
Let me take a photo.

202
00:16:36,740 --> 00:16:38,190
Be serious.

203
00:16:40,170 --> 00:16:41,710
Be serious.

204
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:45,450
['Orad, can you hear me?]

205
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:51,430
This is the last time

206
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:54,510
I'm wasting the film negative on you.

207
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:58,520
I just wanted to take a picture with you.

208
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,360
Is that so hard?

209
00:17:03,490 --> 00:17:05,119
Every single one turns out like this.

210
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:15,810
You're a pig!

211
00:17:17,130 --> 00:17:19,990
You're pig-headed.

212
00:17:21,310 --> 00:17:23,460
Pig-headed.

213
00:17:28,790 --> 00:17:30,020
[Salmon rice ball]

214
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:30,330
'Orad.

215
00:17:36,750 --> 00:17:39,130
You can't bear to see me hungry, right?

216
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:44,580
['Orad, are you there?]

217
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:52,370
'Orad.

218
00:17:53,510 --> 00:17:55,270
Is that you?

219
00:18:07,770 --> 00:18:09,880
I'm not feeling well.

220
00:18:11,110 --> 00:18:14,900
Help me check if I have a fever.

221
00:18:14,990 --> 00:18:16,830
[Good morning, 'Orad.]

222
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:20,790
['Orad, what do you think I should do?]

223
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:21,630
[You're annoying.]

224
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:22,910
That's enough.

225
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:23,650
[You're really annoying, 'Orad.]

226
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:24,800
I beg you.

227
00:18:24,890 --> 00:18:25,330
['Orad.]

228
00:18:25,410 --> 00:18:27,700
Don't show me these things anymore!

229
00:18:33,950 --> 00:18:36,060
Why didn't you keep watching?

230
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:44,510
Is this the answer you wanted to give me?

231
00:18:47,370 --> 00:18:51,370
After I left her,

232
00:18:52,470 --> 00:18:54,230
Hsieh Tien-ti will continue
to lie to herself.

233
00:18:55,950 --> 00:18:58,240
She'll lie to herself
that I'm still by her side.

234
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:00,130
That I never left.

235
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:01,400
Don't you think

236
00:19:01,490 --> 00:19:03,600
that is too cruel to her?

237
00:19:04,570 --> 00:19:05,980
So...

238
00:19:06,110 --> 00:19:08,490
is living in a reality without you

239
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:11,960
less cruel to her?

240
00:19:13,150 --> 00:19:14,600
Is that what you want?

241
00:19:19,050 --> 00:19:20,320
At least

242
00:19:22,130 --> 00:19:24,460
she doesn't have to live in a lie.

243
00:19:37,170 --> 00:19:40,740
Have you ever thought
that in Hsieh Tien-ti's mind,

244
00:19:42,150 --> 00:19:43,950
you're not just a lie?

245
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:46,280
You could be

246
00:19:47,070 --> 00:19:48,700
a wish that she made.

247
00:19:52,220 --> 00:19:55,210
'Orad, close your eyes.

248
00:19:57,370 --> 00:20:00,850
This time, experience it for yourself.

249
00:20:02,610 --> 00:20:04,320
In Hsieh Tien-ti's heart,

250
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:06,960
are you a lie

251
00:20:08,110 --> 00:20:10,440
or a wish she wants to come true?

252
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,400
['Orad.]

253
00:20:43,610 --> 00:20:47,480
'Orad, are you there?

254
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:16,880
I'm not feeling well.

255
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:20,830
Help me check

256
00:21:21,580 --> 00:21:23,780
if I have a fever.

257
00:21:46,660 --> 00:21:48,380
I asked you to come

258
00:21:48,470 --> 00:21:51,020
because I wanted you to treat my cold.

259
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:57,840
But I think this is for the best.

260
00:22:01,010 --> 00:22:02,990
If I'm not well,

261
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:07,780
you'll stay by my side
and take care of me.

262
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:14,430
You're a Kawas anyway.

263
00:22:15,700 --> 00:22:17,770
You can't catch a cold from me.

264
00:22:17,860 --> 00:22:18,600
Am I right?

265
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:27,620
What should I do?

266
00:22:41,090 --> 00:22:42,800
I really like

267
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:46,680
the feeling of having you by my side.

268
00:22:52,350 --> 00:22:57,590
I really like it a lot.

269
00:23:32,650 --> 00:23:37,010
'Orad, good morning.

270
00:23:38,150 --> 00:23:40,090
Good morning.

271
00:23:56,460 --> 00:23:57,780
[Putting aside the water shortage,]

272
00:23:57,870 --> 00:24:01,170
[the White Algae Disorder
is getting worse too.]

273
00:24:01,250 --> 00:24:04,770
It's okay. There will be another time.

274
00:24:05,130 --> 00:24:07,110
Okay, thank you. Bye.

275
00:24:09,530 --> 00:24:11,590
There goes another case.

276
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:14,190
What should I do?

277
00:24:14,320 --> 00:24:15,020
If this continues,

278
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:16,610
I think our company will go bankrupt.

279
00:24:16,780 --> 00:24:18,940
It's okay. We're in a difficult time.

280
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:20,390
Last week...

281
00:24:24,570 --> 00:24:26,160
Why didn't you remind me?

282
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:29,100
People might think I'm talking to myself.

283
00:24:29,240 --> 00:24:31,350
You don't have to care
about what other people think.

284
00:24:31,920 --> 00:24:33,330
I'm right here.

285
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:35,790
Okay.

286
00:24:38,340 --> 00:24:39,400
Forget it.

287
00:24:39,530 --> 00:24:41,860
I don't want to talk about work.
It's annoying.

288
00:24:43,580 --> 00:24:45,910
Let's watch a movie later, okay?

289
00:24:46,750 --> 00:24:48,420
Okay.

290
00:24:48,990 --> 00:24:50,220
When we go to the movies,

291
00:24:50,310 --> 00:24:52,290
should I just buy one ticket?

292
00:24:52,380 --> 00:24:54,140
What about the person sitting next to you?

293
00:24:54,230 --> 00:24:55,330
Right.

294
00:24:55,420 --> 00:24:56,820
That's bothersome.

295
00:24:58,320 --> 00:24:59,640
Ma'am.

296
00:24:59,730 --> 00:25:01,270
Ma'am, are you okay?

297
00:25:02,370 --> 00:25:03,160
Tien-ti.

298
00:25:03,290 --> 00:25:04,830
Can someone help?

299
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:06,990
Mister, come and help.

300
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:08,350
Call for help.

301
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:10,990
There are kids here. Come and help.

302
00:25:11,080 --> 00:25:12,490
Ma'am, are you okay?

303
00:25:12,580 --> 00:25:13,940
Don't cry.

304
00:25:14,030 --> 00:25:15,210
It's okay.

305
00:25:15,350 --> 00:25:17,990
It's okay.

306
00:25:18,120 --> 00:25:19,610
It's okay.

307
00:25:46,010 --> 00:25:47,110
No!

308
00:25:48,300 --> 00:25:49,230
No...

309
00:25:51,950 --> 00:25:53,540
Take me back now.

310
00:25:53,630 --> 00:25:54,020
I need to save her.

311
00:25:54,110 --> 00:25:54,860
Have you forgotten?

312
00:25:55,650 --> 00:25:57,190
What you just saw

313
00:25:57,320 --> 00:25:58,820
is the Reflection of Time of the future.

314
00:26:00,010 --> 00:26:00,620
How are you going

315
00:26:00,750 --> 00:26:02,380
to save Hsieh Tien-ti
in the Reflection of Time

316
00:26:02,780 --> 00:26:03,920
that hasn't happened yet?

317
00:26:05,590 --> 00:26:06,470
Moreover,

318
00:26:07,270 --> 00:26:08,060
didn't you

319
00:26:08,150 --> 00:26:10,130
previously deny your own existence?

320
00:26:11,970 --> 00:26:15,010
So how will you
who don't exist in the future

321
00:26:15,760 --> 00:26:17,520
save Hsieh Tien-ti?

322
00:26:17,650 --> 00:26:19,580
I can't, but you can.

323
00:26:20,020 --> 00:26:22,310
You're the almighty Kakarayan.

324
00:26:22,750 --> 00:26:24,120
This is all part of your plan.

325
00:26:24,250 --> 00:26:25,610
You can change all this.

326
00:26:29,090 --> 00:26:30,630
If I do as you say

327
00:26:31,770 --> 00:26:33,710
and change the future that I've arranged,

328
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:37,010
does that mean

329
00:26:37,930 --> 00:26:40,350
I've regretted my decision?

330
00:26:50,910 --> 00:26:51,750
'Orad.

331
00:26:52,760 --> 00:26:54,780
You're my messenger.

332
00:26:54,920 --> 00:26:57,910
After millennia, do you still remember

333
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:00,720
why the word "sorry" doesn't exist

334
00:27:01,470 --> 00:27:03,010
in the language of the Kawas?

335
00:27:05,080 --> 00:27:06,930
Because the Kawas are not human.

336
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:11,190
A Kawas doesn't do anything he'll regret.

337
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:12,780
That's right.

338
00:27:14,670 --> 00:27:16,610
As Kakarayan,

339
00:27:16,690 --> 00:27:18,450
I have no right to regret anything.

340
00:27:19,950 --> 00:27:21,310
What if today,

341
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:24,390
I regret something

342
00:27:24,970 --> 00:27:26,730
and change something else?

343
00:27:28,930 --> 00:27:30,470
What if one day,

344
00:27:32,530 --> 00:27:35,440
I regret creating humans

345
00:27:36,010 --> 00:27:38,300
and creating this world?

346
00:27:40,320 --> 00:27:41,690
What should I do then?

347
00:27:45,600 --> 00:27:46,390
So...

348
00:27:49,080 --> 00:27:51,500
when you lost the one you loved,

349
00:27:53,700 --> 00:27:55,190
you couldn't regret it

350
00:27:56,160 --> 00:27:58,320
and couldn't change the future
where she was no longer in.

351
00:27:58,410 --> 00:27:59,200
But you didn't know

352
00:27:59,290 --> 00:28:00,830
how to fill the hole in your heart.

353
00:28:05,230 --> 00:28:06,630
So you created me.

354
00:28:08,660 --> 00:28:10,330
You made up this lie

355
00:28:10,990 --> 00:28:12,000
so that I could do the things

356
00:28:12,090 --> 00:28:13,410
you couldn't do yourself.

357
00:28:18,290 --> 00:28:19,920
Hsieh Tien-ti was right.

358
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:22,960
You're just an irresponsible
good-for-nothing.

359
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:28,190
If you can't make mistakes as Kakarayan,

360
00:28:28,500 --> 00:28:29,200
then fine.

361
00:28:29,640 --> 00:28:31,620
It's okay.
I'll make mistakes on your behalf.

362
00:28:32,500 --> 00:28:33,650
I'll lie for you.

363
00:28:33,780 --> 00:28:34,620
I'll do the things

364
00:28:34,750 --> 00:28:36,070
you couldn't do yourself.

365
00:28:36,160 --> 00:28:37,920
If you can't feel regret,

366
00:28:39,020 --> 00:28:40,160
let me regret it for you.

367
00:28:40,730 --> 00:28:41,700
I regret it.

368
00:28:43,020 --> 00:28:45,530
I regret denying my own existence.

369
00:28:46,450 --> 00:28:47,600
Are you happy now?

370
00:28:50,280 --> 00:28:51,780
If you give me one more chance

371
00:28:53,100 --> 00:28:54,810
to remain with Hsieh Tien-ti,

372
00:28:56,130 --> 00:28:56,790
I don't care

373
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:58,730
if you make me the lie
to deceive yourself.

374
00:28:58,820 --> 00:29:00,090
Will that do?

375
00:29:07,040 --> 00:29:08,270
You finally understand

376
00:29:09,420 --> 00:29:11,880
why I arranged for you
and Hsieh Tien-ti to meet.

377
00:29:17,690 --> 00:29:19,980
It's because only Hsieh Tien-ti
can show you

378
00:29:21,030 --> 00:29:23,100
that she and I believe you to be real.

379
00:29:27,150 --> 00:29:28,430
For me,

380
00:29:30,320 --> 00:29:32,030
you were never a lie.

381
00:29:35,070 --> 00:29:37,090
You were a wish I prayed for sincerely.

382
00:29:39,650 --> 00:29:41,050
A wish that I hoped

383
00:29:41,980 --> 00:29:43,780
would come true one day.

384
00:30:52,160 --> 00:30:53,080
[I am...]

385
00:30:56,160 --> 00:30:57,700
[a wish you prayed for.]

386
00:30:59,590 --> 00:31:01,620
After losing Tiyamacan,

387
00:31:04,030 --> 00:31:05,050
I realized something.

388
00:31:06,100 --> 00:31:09,050
As Kakarayan who could do everything,

389
00:31:10,500 --> 00:31:11,870
the only thing I couldn't do

390
00:31:13,450 --> 00:31:15,210
was to be a human

391
00:31:17,100 --> 00:31:21,020
and choose her amidst so many people.

392
00:31:21,940 --> 00:31:23,090
To love only her,

393
00:31:24,140 --> 00:31:25,810
protect her,

394
00:31:27,050 --> 00:31:28,670
and grow old with her.

395
00:31:38,930 --> 00:31:40,030
My messenger.

396
00:31:44,470 --> 00:31:47,860
I was wondering if you would replace me

397
00:31:49,440 --> 00:31:51,770
to do what I could never do.

398
00:31:53,710 --> 00:31:54,720
Take my place

399
00:31:56,040 --> 00:31:58,950
and make my wish come true.

400
00:32:15,050 --> 00:32:16,320
Well then,

401
00:32:18,300 --> 00:32:19,760
let us

402
00:32:20,500 --> 00:32:22,130
realize this wish together.

403
00:32:37,530 --> 00:32:38,280
Hey.

404
00:32:38,680 --> 00:32:39,640
Guardian angel.

405
00:32:41,320 --> 00:32:43,210
This is really the last one.

406
00:32:46,160 --> 00:32:49,370
Can you promise me one thing?

407
00:32:55,750 --> 00:32:57,020
Can you

408
00:32:59,570 --> 00:33:01,250
not erase my memory?

409
00:33:11,320 --> 00:33:13,300
[I don't know when I started]

410
00:33:15,060 --> 00:33:17,700
[to have this feeling.]

411
00:33:20,430 --> 00:33:24,260
[I feel like I've forgotten something]

412
00:33:24,960 --> 00:33:27,870
[that is very, very important to me.]

413
00:33:30,680 --> 00:33:32,570
[I've been trying hard to remember.]

414
00:33:32,710 --> 00:33:34,110
[But I can't remember anything.]

415
00:33:37,810 --> 00:33:38,910
[Until...]

416
00:33:41,680 --> 00:33:42,870
[I met you again.]

417
00:33:50,310 --> 00:33:51,890
[Then I remembered]

418
00:33:53,210 --> 00:33:55,320
[the important thing]

419
00:33:55,410 --> 00:33:56,550
[that I've been]

420
00:33:58,000 --> 00:33:59,410
[looking for.]

421
00:34:09,880 --> 00:34:10,500
I don't want...

422
00:34:10,590 --> 00:34:11,469
Me neither.

423
00:34:15,300 --> 00:34:17,190
I've never forgotten about it.

424
00:34:16,570 --> 00:34:23,219
♫ In the last second,
I just want to be with you ♫

425
00:34:23,570 --> 00:34:30,520
♫ Letting my emotions show,
admitting that I'm weak ♫

426
00:34:30,610 --> 00:34:39,100
♫ There's no need to pretend you're cool,
why taint the memories? ♫

427
00:34:39,409 --> 00:34:44,639
♫ I just want to tell you
the promise I didn't say ♫

428
00:34:44,730 --> 00:34:46,840
♫ In the last second ♫

429
00:34:46,929 --> 00:34:49,620
♫ Time is slipping away ♫

430
00:34:49,699 --> 00:34:52,960
♫ We can't go back, we can't start over ♫

431
00:34:53,050 --> 00:34:59,030
♫ In the end,
the promise has turned into pain ♫

432
00:34:59,290 --> 00:35:05,370
♫ We're in love, but we're afraid
of the end and missing out ♫

433
00:35:05,450 --> 00:35:12,890
♫ It's no use regretting it,
it won't bring back your tenderness ♫

434
00:35:13,020 --> 00:35:21,430
♫ There's no need to pretend you're cool,
why taint the memories? ♫

435
00:35:21,870 --> 00:35:27,190
♫ I just want to tell you
the promise I didn't say ♫

436
00:35:27,450 --> 00:35:31,330
♫ In the last second ♫

437
00:36:39,660 --> 00:36:41,240
Lemed.

438
00:36:44,410 --> 00:36:46,960
I've already fulfilled

439
00:36:47,050 --> 00:36:48,630
the wish I made.

440
00:36:53,950 --> 00:36:56,950
I was wondering if you'd like to join me

441
00:36:58,090 --> 00:36:59,850
to fulfill my next wish.
